      "id": "t016021",
      "source": "Problem 922. Population balance in a town: case 2",
      "translation": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "t016022",
      "source": "Knowledge context.",
      "translation": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "t016023",
      "source": "Population changes through births, deaths, immigration, and emigration.",
      "translation": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "t016024",
      "source": "Given facts.",
      "translation": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "t016025",
      "source": "A town begins the year with 1450 residents. During the year: births=23, deaths=14, people moving in=38, people moving out=29.",
      "translation": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "t016026",
      "source": "Rules.",
      "translation": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "t016027",
      "source": "End population = start + births − deaths + in-migration − out-migration. Natural change and migration change are separate components.",
      "translation": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "t016028",
      "source": "Task.",
      "translation": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "t016029",
      "source": "Compute natural change, migration change, and the year-end population.",
      "translation": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "t016030",
      "source": "Step-by-step solution.",
      "translation": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "t016031",
      "source": "1. Natural change=23−14=9. 2. Migration change=38−29=9. 3. Total change=9+9=18. 4. End population=1450+18=1468.",
      "translation": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "t016032",
      "source": "Answer.",
      "translation": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "t016033",
      "source": "Natural change +9; migration change +9; end population 1468.",
      "translation": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "t016034",
      "source": "Knowledge takeaway.",
      "translation": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "t016035",
      "source": "Breaking total change into components helps explain why a population grew or shrank.",
      "translation": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "t016036",
      "source": "Formal model.",
      "translation": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "t016037",
      "source": "Balance equation P1=P0+births−deaths+in−out.",
      "translation": ""
    },
